From 4e316bc085a86c9dcd6ee7df62752e34810fdb95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:11:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): G41/G42 cutter compensation on Haas, Mazak and
 Siemens 840D

Haas and Mazak write the Fanuc-family words on the next straight feed
block (G1/G01 G41|G42 ... D<tool>, G40 on the lead-out); Siemens 840D
writes G1 G41|G42 NORM with the radius from the edge the tool call
already selected (T n D n). The Fanuc post's laws carry over: a comp
word on a rapid, an arc or past the section end, or inside a canned
cycle, is a named refusal that blocks the gate; wear (#38) writes one
register note per section. Heidenhain keeps its by-name refusal - its
documented engage point is not stated against the next element, and
its radius is always R plus DR (docs/decisions/39-comp-dialects.md).

Goldens: golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/contour_{control,wear}_comp.nc.

Fixes #39

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
